<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.Africa money mkt shortage falls to 10.4 bln rand.</title>
<headline>S.Africa money mkt shortage falls to 10.4 bln rand.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-01-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's money market shortage stood at 10.448 billion rand on Tuesday, down from 10.737 billion rand on Monday, the Reserve Bank said on Thursday.</p>
<p>On December 27, the shortage touched a record high of 11.126 billion rand.</p>
<p>Three-month NCD rates were steady at between 17.40 and 17.75 percent while the 90-day BA rate was also unchanged at 16.70 to 17.00 percent.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom, +27 11 482-1003</p>
